; The M03 bench. WO-0038 built the clean-frame spine of Xgmii_rx_64;
; later packets extend it, and this header is a standing list rather than
; a snapshot of the first one (RV-0040-R5: it read "eleven rows" from
; WO-0038 until 2026-08-07, having gone stale at M03-C5 and staler at
; family D — the same left-standing-summary defect that cost a campaign
; finding at RV-0039-VERDICT F-2 and put a banner on AP-xgmii_rx_64.md §7).
;
; AP-xgmii_rx_64.md rows live here, by packet:
;   WO-0038  A1-A5, B1, C1-C4, L6           (eleven)
;   WO-0038 round 6 / BUG-0001  C5          (one)
;   WO-0040  D1-D3 ASSERT, D4 declared      (four)
;   WO-0043  E1, E2, E4 ASSERT, E3 declared (three ASSERT + one declared)
;   WO-0047  F1-F4 ASSERT, F5 by citation to test_m03_c.ml's C4;
;            E5 ASSERT, folded in but living beside its own family in
;            test_m03_e.ml, not here (four ASSERT + one citation + one ASSERT)
;   WO-0054  G1-G4, G6 ASSERT, G5 declared  (five ASSERT + one declared)
;   WO-0056  G7, G8 ASSERT (first-epoch repair, RV-0056-VERDICT ACCEPT) (two)
;   WO-0057  H1-H4 ASSERT (start without terminate, REQ-110)          (four)
;   WO-0059  I1-I4, I6 ASSERT, I5 declared (silence, ordered sets,
;            idle-injection wrapper, REQ-109/REQ-113/REQ-016) (five ASSERT
;            + one declared)
;   WO-0062  B2-B4 ASSERT (the preamble as an attack surface, REQ-102;
;            REQ-110's commissioned lane-4-of-an-S-word geometry, WO-0058
;            §9 bound 6; B1 untouched)                             (three)
; When a packet adds rows, add its line. When one does not, this comment
; is wrong and a reader has no way to tell — this file's own header found
; that exact staleness (E and F both missing) before WO-0054's own line was
; added, and both are repaired in the same edit rather than left standing.
;
; Depends on hardcaml_ethernet (the design under test — REQ-010's
; type-identity check does its job if the ports diverge from
; docs/specs/ifc_check/xgmii_rx_64_ifc.ml). tools/precompile_check.sh's
; STUBBABLE set does not cover it, so this directory is EXCLUDED from that
; harness by construction (WO-0038 §6 rule 2) and CI's `dune build @default`
; is the only compiler that reaches it (ADR-0005).
;
; RV-0038 addendum D1 (J-dv_lead-0023): hardcaml_waveterm was dropped from
; this stanza along with bench.ml's `waves` field — the field was written
; (Waveform.create) and never read, costing a full per-cycle waveform
; recording (~43 elaborations in this packet) for a capability no test here
; uses. Add hardcaml_waveterm back in the packet that first needs a waveform
; expectation.
;
; dv_xgmii, dv_xgmii_probe, dv_axi64_probe and dv_monitors are the
; DUT-independent machinery named in WO-0038 §3: the link-partner schedule
; and frame builder, the XGMII drive/sample seam, the Axi64 sample seam, and
; the standing monitors (protocol, conservation, strobe). None of
; libs/hardcaml_ethernet/src/xgmii_rx_64.ml or rtl_snapshots/** was opened
; to write anything in this directory (PROTOCOL §10, WO-0038 §5) — bench.ml
; reaches the DUT's ports only through the field names SPEC-M03 §4.1 and
; the WO itself state, via type-directed record-field projection, never by
; naming the concrete module that defines them.
;
; ifc_check is not a dependency: bench.ml drives and samples the DUT's ports
; via Bits.t ref projection (Xgmii_probe.to_refs / Axi64_probe.of_refs), not
; via the Ifc_check.Axi64_ifc types, so it needs no opinion about whether
; hardcaml_ethernet's Xgmii/Axi64 records are literally that library's types
; or structurally identical ones of their own.
;
; ppx_hardcaml ppx_jane ppx_expect, matching test/hardcaml_ethernet/dune —
; this is the one directory in this packet that touches Signal.t/Bits.t and
; needs Base's operators alongside Hardcaml's ppx.

(library
 (name test_xgmii_rx_64)
 (inline_tests)
 (libraries hardcaml hardcaml_ethernet dv_xgmii dv_xgmii_probe dv_axi64_probe dv_monitors)
 (preprocess
  (pps ppx_hardcaml ppx_jane ppx_expect)))
